WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.669
- All right, y'all, we are back
with the one and only, Pink.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:06.000
Give it up!
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.460
So, we are both big fans of my next guest.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:10.110
He's an artist who works with musicians

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.170
to create one of a kind pieces
depicted in sound waves,

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.190
which is super rad.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.500
Check out Sam Smith's "Stay With me."

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.940
That is so cool.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.490
Then there's Celine Dion's
"My Heart Will Go On."

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.390
- [Pink] Oh, that's beautiful.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.830
- [Kelly] Everyone's still
wondering why she's not

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:24.300
in the top 200, it's okay.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.475
And look at this one.

00:00:26.475 --> 00:00:29.174
This is Pink's own, "So What."

00:00:29.174 --> 00:00:30.960
(audience cheering)

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.910
But this art isn't just beautiful, y'all.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.580
It also helped raise nearly $7 million

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:36.960
for truly worthy charities.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:37.887
Let's welcome the creator

00:00:37.887 --> 00:00:40.380
of Soundwaves Art Foundation, Tim.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.635
Give it up for Tim, y'all.

00:00:41.635 --> 00:00:43.848
(audience cheering)

00:00:43.848 --> 00:00:45.240
So it's great to meet you.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.950
I know that y'all have
worked together a little bit

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:47.910
because I saw photos.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.860
And I know that y'all worked together.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.510
So how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.950
This is such a rad idea.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.070
- So 15 years ago, I was a a music lover

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.810
and a fundraiser in London.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.930
And I had this crazy idea
that I could become an artist

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:04.650
by capturing what essentially
is the heartbeat of a song

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.870
that you see in recording
studios all the time.

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:08.280
Those images that you see.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.140
- Yeah.
- So I created some artwork

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.090
for Coldplay from "Yellow"

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.890
and I drove down to London in my truck.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.980
And there isn't a sign
that says Coldplay Studio.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:18.690
So I mean, I'm driving through London

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:20.940
and I find the alleyway
where it's supposed to be.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.530
And I blocked the alleyway

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:24.330
and I'm looking for this studio

00:01:24.330 --> 00:01:25.920
and this young guy comes along on a bike

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.640
and he takes three minutes to
lift the bike over my truck

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:30.480
and then puts it down.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.800
And I'm just got my head, and I'm like,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.750
I can't believe how embarrassing this is.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.490
And I said, "Do you know
where Coldplay Studio is?"

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.780
And he says, "Yeah, I work here."

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.287
And he opened the door and I said,

00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:40.680
"Could I leave some artwork
here for them to look at?"

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.970
And he took off his bike helmet

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.893
and it was Chris Martin from Coldplay.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.170
- I was like, you know
what, I know the place.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:47.400
Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.870
- I thought these guys
are never gonna sign.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.790
So, but they're the
nicest guys in the world.

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:52.740
And they started the whole thing rolling.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.190
And 15 years later, we've
had an amazing journey, so.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.260
- That's my daughter's
favorite Coldplay song,

00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.397
is "Yellow."

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.420
So now you work with hundreds

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:03.990
of the world's most notable artists.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.910
So what's the process like?

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.470
- Essentially, we go to artists usually

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.480
who are touring in London or Austin,

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:10.950
'cause that's where we're based.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.990
And we'll ask 'em if they
have a social justice issue

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:14.253
that they wanna support.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.320
They'll choose a song,

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.140
and then I'll create
artwork from that song.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.690
They'll then sign limited edition print

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.220
and original canvases,

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.470
and then they post it
on their social media.

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:27.990
And then their fans have
access to buy those.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.180
A hundred percent of the
profit goes to charity.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.530
So for instance, last year,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.150
when the Ukrainian crisis started,

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.570
we reached out to musicians
who spoke about the issue,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:39.360
like Barbara Streisand,
Robert Smith from The Cure,

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:40.200
the Pet Shop Boys.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.005
And we've raised $600,000 just for,

00:02:44.005 --> 00:02:45.245
thank you, thank you.

00:02:45.245 --> 00:02:46.643
(audience cheering)

00:02:46.643 --> 00:02:50.370
So Children in Conflict,
they provide safe spaces

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:53.730
for children who've
fled Ukraine, you know,

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.380
a lot of them have lost their parents.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.670
- Lost everything.
- They're alone.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.030
So they give them not
just food and education,

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:01.860
but counseling and
helping to come to terms

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:02.790
with what they've gone through.

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.050
So, that's-

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.790
- And will continue to go through. Yeah.

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.680
- So yeah, we're continuing
to do that this year.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.600
And we are pledging 50,000 a month

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:11.913
to help keep safe spaces
open in the Ukraine.

00:03:12.817 --> 00:03:14.460
- That's so cool.
- Thank you.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.490
- So tell us what happened
when you reached out to Pink.

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.770
- So you've been on my
radar for a long time

00:03:19.770 --> 00:03:22.080
and then you were
announced as the headliner

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.610
for Austin City Limits.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.620
So we reached out to your team

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:27.607
and they came back with three songs.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.370
"So what," "Just Give Me a Reason"

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.990
and "Cover Me In Sunshine."

00:03:30.990 --> 00:03:33.060
And I created the artwork for you.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.180
And gotta tell you, we've
worked with 500 musicians

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:38.550
in 15 years and when you posted,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:40.590
it was the fastest selling
artwork we've ever had.

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.845
- Yay.
(audience cheering)

00:03:41.845 --> 00:03:44.300
- There's like a few people
like her, like there's a few.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.860
- We raised $40,000 in two hours

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:48.570
for No Kid Hungry and Unicef.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.500
- Oh my gosh.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.860
- We have a wait list of a thousand people

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:53.940
who want your artwork.

00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:54.840
- Will you make more?

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.310
- Okay, anytime you like.
- Nice.

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:57.720
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.250
- But the best part of
it is that you asked

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.263
for an original piece-

00:04:00.263 --> 00:04:01.096
- Yes, I did.

00:04:01.096 --> 00:04:02.245
- And I hope you got it in your house.

00:04:02.245 --> 00:04:03.541
- I do.
- And I hope you treasure it.

00:04:03.541 --> 00:04:04.374
- I love it.

00:04:04.374 --> 00:04:05.520
- It's been a pleasure and a privilege.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:06.720
I've gotta be honest.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.830
- That's so cool, man.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.663
- Yeah. Thank you.

00:04:08.663 --> 00:04:09.840
- All right, well, I'm excited

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.270
because I'm part of Tim's latest creation

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:15.960
and fundraising effort which
is right beneath this cloth.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.480
It's an image of a song that I love.

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.620
It's called "Broken and Beautiful."

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.170
It's a song that I
recorded, but Pink wrote.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.111
So I thought it would
be a perfect song to do.

00:04:25.111 --> 00:04:26.370
(audience cheering)

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:28.170
I cannot wait to show it to the world.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:29.910
Okay, so remove the
cover. I'll let you do it.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.990
Or do you want me to help or you got it?

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.325
Okay.
- Good.

00:04:32.325 --> 00:04:35.481
(audience cheering)

00:04:35.481 --> 00:04:37.474
- [Pink] Oh, it's gorgeous.

00:04:37.474 --> 00:04:38.891
- This is so rad.

00:04:40.132 --> 00:04:43.710
This piece is going up for
auction today for just one week.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.920
I'm thinking about
buying it myself (laughs)

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:50.340
and the proceeds will benefit
No Kid Hungry, everybody.

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:51.780
But first, we have to sign it.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.930
So of course, we are gonna use
a Pilot silver paint marker.

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.610
As you know, Pilot is the maker of G2,

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:57.990
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.670
If you didn't know that, well, you should.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:01.500
They like to celebrate unstoppable artists

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.090
just like Tim and us.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:03.923
So you wanna go first?

00:05:03.923 --> 00:05:05.190
- Sure.
- All right.

00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:06.023
- Where do you wanna sign?

00:05:06.023 --> 00:05:07.530
- [Pink] Where do you want the signatures?

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.640
- It's kind of fabulous.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.540
- It's beautiful.

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.380
- I'm gonna bet on it.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.917
- Signatures look really
lovely at the bottom-

00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:13.200
- Okay.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.033
Okay.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.217
- If y'all see this in my
house in some photo (laughs).

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.163
Okay.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.420
See, so Pink is athletic.
(audience cheering)

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.420
So, Pink is athletic.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.850
So I was thinking I was
gonna sign over here

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:33.960
but I'm pulling a squat
in my Spanx and my dress.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.600
Here we go, just kidding. Here we go.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.550
- [Pink] That's beautiful.

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.050
- [Kelly] Boop, boop, boop.

00:05:40.050 --> 00:05:42.250
Okay, and I'm getting up on my heel.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.030
All right, everybody.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:48.060
To bid on this piece and
support No Kid Hungry,

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.730
just go to The Kelly Clarkson
Show's Instagram right now.

00:05:50.730 --> 00:05:52.350
It's for a good cause and good news,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.720
everyone in the audience,
y'all are actually going home

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.966
with a print of "Broken and Beautiful."

00:05:56.966 --> 00:05:59.428
(audience cheering)

